The finite deletion induction in FINITE-LOG1603 is valid for arbitrary complex activities throughout its fixed closed polydisc, under its self-including incompatibility budget. The translation in DOBRUSHIN-DICTIONARY1604 satisfies the selected Dobrushin criterion in the pinned author-hosted exposition. That selected theorem supplies the stated absolute logarithmic cluster bounds, including the original-label root bound and the separately budgeted additional size weight. I found no invalid displayed inequality, missing self term, lost enumeration factorial, or material error in these two conditional deductions.

